mh2lm: trace lock-screen battery transition contract (0126)

0112m20 confirms that PM8150B charging continues while the current
framebuffer-only display-off state is active. The missing plug-in charging
animation is therefore not a charge-current failure. Before implementing any
PMIC IRQ or AppleSmartBatteryManager ABI behaviour, record the exact standard
IOPM source transition and every battery user-client call that occurs during a
controlled lock-screen plug/unplug sequence.

Under the new opt-in `sweetbattuidiag=1` argument, log only externally visible
source transitions (external, capable, charging or full) immediately before
and after the existing `updateStatus()` call. Also log every user-client
external method while the option is active, including its first scalar input.
Without the argument, the existing once-per-selector user-client trace remains
unchanged.

This is diagnostics only: it performs no PMIC write, does not enable or clear
an IRQ, does not change a user-client return value, and does not request a
display power transition. Existing `SWEET FB: display off/on` markers provide
the display-side correlation for the resulting persistent log.

